.TH LXMF-CHAT 1 "March 2026" "lxmf-cli-chat" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lxmf-chat \- LXMF terminal chat client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lxmf-chat
[\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-identity\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-\-send-to\fR \fIHEX\fR \fB\-\-msg\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlxmf-chat\fR is an interactive TUI and headless CLI sender for LXMF over Reticulum.
When started without \fB\-\-send-to\fR and \fB\-\-msg\fR, it runs the full terminal UI.
When both are provided, it sends one message and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-name NAME
Set display name. Default: \fBAnonymous\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-config DIR
Use a custom Reticulum configuration directory.
.TP
.B \-\-identity FILE
Use a custom Reticulum identity file.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to file.
.TP
.B \-\-send-to HEX
Recipient destination hash for one-shot non-interactive send mode.
.TP
.B \-\-msg TEXT
Message content used with \fB\-\-send-to\fR.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B /t, /target <hex>
Set destination by full or partial hash.
.TP
.B /c, /chat [idx]
Switch active session, or cycle sessions if no index is provided.
.TP
.B /r, /reply [msg]
Reply to the most recent conversation.
.TP
.B /p, /peers
Browse discovered peers.
.TP
.B /s, /search <query>
Search peers by name or hash.
.TP
.B /n, /name <name>
Set display name.
.TP
.B /a, /announce
Send network announce.
.TP
.B /sf, /sendfile <path>
Send file attachment to current target.
.TP
.B /id
Show own destination hash.
.TP
.B /mode <direct|propagated|auto>
Set delivery mode.
.TP
.B /pn <hex|auto|list|fetch>
Manage propagation node selection and fetch behavior.
.TP
.B /stamp <1-255>
Set required inbound stamp cost.
.TP
.B /grant [hex], /ticket
Send a message and grant a one-time ticket.
.TP
.B /block <hex>
Block destination hash.
.TP
.B /unblock <hex>
Unblock destination hash.
.TP
.B /blocked
List blocked destination hashes.
.TP
.B /manual, /help
Show in-app command manual.
.TP
.B /q, /quit
Exit.
.SH TUI SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl-P
Toggle peer list mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
Cycle active chats.
.TP
.B Ctrl-A
Trigger announce.
.TP
.B Ctrl-L
Redraw screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Q
Quit.
.TP
.B Esc
Return to chat mode.
.TP
.B PageUp/PageDown
Scroll chat history.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run interactive TUI:
.B lxmf-chat --name "MyName"
.TP
Send one message and exit:
.B lxmf-chat --send-to 7cc8d66b4f6a0e0e49d34af7f6077b5a --msg "Hello"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.lxmf_cli_chat
Application data root (identity, local router state, logs, downloads).
.TP
.I ~/.lxmf_cli_chat/router/lxmf
LXMF router storage (tickets, stamp costs, propagation state).
.TP
.I ~/.lxmf_cli_chat/downloads
Received file attachments.
.TP
.I ~/.reticulum
Default Reticulum config location (unless \fB\-\-config\fR is set).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rnsd (1)
